   ["Adequate iron stores for inflammation",
    "Ferritin is an acute phase reactant, so with a C-reactive protein of 4.8 mg/dL it should be normal or high; a value of 21 ng/mL is low for this setting. Tell: below 30 ng/mL in chronic disease means stores are short.", "reversed direction or value"],
